/-!
# The inputs of Tag 0A0L's missing step, for the derived completion along a quasi-coherent ideal

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme, `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_X` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals and `K` an
object of `D(𝒪_X)`. [Stacks, Tag 0A0L] computes, over an affine open `U` with `A = Γ(X, U)` and
`I = ℐ(U)`,

`H^p(U, K^∧) = lim H^p(U, K)/IⁿH^p(U, K)`,

and `Completion/FormalFunctionsPseudoCoherentModuleSide.lean` proves it with the left-hand side
read on the module side — at the derived completion in `D(A)` of `RΓ(U, K)` — keeping as an input,
in `exists_adjunction_and_homology_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_iso_adicCompletion`, an object
`Kc` of `D(𝒪_X)` and an isomorphism `RΓ(U, Kc) ≅ RΓ(U, K)^∧`. That input is the one step of the
source's proof passing between `RΓ(U, K^∧)` and `RΓ(U, K)^∧`, namely [Stacks, Tag 0CQI].

This file provides the three identifications that step needs, each of which the documentation of
this subtree records as unavailable.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection_eq_globalSectionOfTerminalSection` — the
  two readings of a section over `U` as a global section of `𝒪_U` agree. This is what turns the
  generating family of `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_affine`
  into the shape [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] consumes.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.derivedSectionsOverObject_eq_derivedSections` — **the ringed-site model
  of `RΓ(U, -)` that [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] is stated in and the ringed-space model that
  [Stacks, Tag 0A0L] is stated in are the same functor**, by `rfl`, on the small Zariski site of
  a scheme. Both are the total right derived functor of sections over `U` with values in modules
  over `Γ(X, U)`; the module documentation of `Completion/AdicQuotientDerivedLimit.lean` named
  their comparison as what part (2) still waits on, and it is an identity.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.cechCompletionFunctor_iso_compι` — **every left adjoint of the inclusion
  of the derived-complete objects of `D(A)`, composed with that inclusion, is the Čech completion
  functor** of [Stacks, Tag 091V] at a finite family spanning the ideal. [Stacks, Tag 0A0L]
  quantifies over every such left adjoint while [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] produces the Čech model, and
  this is what makes the two meet.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealSheafSiteSubmodule` — the
  derived completion functor along the tag's own ideal sheaf, as an instance, so that `K^∧` can
  be written down in a statement about a locally Noetherian scheme.

## The ideals agree too

[Stacks, Tag 0CQI] is along the ideal `(f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ A` generated by the chosen sections, which
the source warns need not be `ℐ(U)`. On an affine open of a locally Noetherian scheme the
sections can be chosen to span `ℐ(U)` exactly —
`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_affine` — so no mismatch has to
be carried, and the ideal of [Stacks, Tag 0A0L] and the ideal of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] are the same
ideal here.

## What assembling these still costs

Composing them is elaboration work rather than mathematics, and it is not done here: the
statement that names `RΓ(U, K^∧)`, the Čech completion of `RΓ(U, K)` and the span of the chosen
family at once exhausts the elaborator's budget, because `Γ(X, U)` and the site's
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionRing` are definitionally but not syntactically equal and
every occurrence pays for the crossing. Splitting that statement, or stating it at one spelling
throughout with the crossing confined to `derivedSectionsOverObject_eq_derivedSections`, is what
remains; no further mathematical input is needed.

## What part (2) needs, and what it does not

Part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] — `H^q(K^∧) = lim H^q(K)/ℐⁿH^q(K)` as **sheaves** — does *not*
need the hypercohomology edge morphism at `K^∧`. It is true that
`Stacks.Cohomology.AcyclicOpen.isIso_hypercohomologyEdge_app_of_isBasis` identifies
`H^q(U, K^∧)` with `Γ(U, H^q(K^∧))` only once the cohomology sheaves of `K^∧` are acyclic over
the affine opens, which they are not known to be — the formal completion of a coherent module is
not quasi-coherent. That concerns the edge morphism and is irrelevant to part (2), because the
cohomology sheaf never has to be evaluated: by
`Stacks.Cohomology.HypercohomologyEdge.sheafificationCohomologyPresheafIso`, which carries no
acyclicity hypothesis at all, `H^q(K^∧)` **is** the sheafification of the hypercohomology
presheaf `U ↦ H^q(U, K^∧)`. So the affine-section statement feeds part (2) by sheafification, and
the acyclicity of the cohomology sheaves of `K^∧` is a consequence of part (2) rather than an
input to it.

The real obstruction is a different one, and it is *naturality in `U`*. Sheafification consumes
a morphism of presheaves, and gluing on a basis
(`Stacks.BasisRestriction.moduleSheafIsoOfSectionIsoOnBasis`) consumes a compatible family; the
affine-section statement of [Stacks, Tag 0A0L] is stated as `Nonempty (… ≅ …)` separately for
each `U`, with no compatibility with restriction, and a family of non-canonical isomorphisms
sheafifies to nothing. Making [Stacks, Tag 0A0L] natural is *not* the only way to supply this:
the two canonical maps of [Stacks, Tag 0CQH] — `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicQuotientReduction`
and `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionAdicFactor` — are global morphisms of
`D(𝒪_X)`, so applying `RΓ(U, -)` and `H^q` to them yields comparisons with the tower
`n ↦ H^q(U, K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ)` that are natural in `U` for free. Part (2) then reduces to those two
comparisons being invertible over an affine open, which is where the Noetherian and
pseudo-coherence hypotheses are spent.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 091V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/091V)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction Stacks.Cohomology.HypercohomologyEdge

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

/-- **The two readings of a section over `U` as a global section of `𝒪_U` agree**: through
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection`, which restricts the section along each
arrow of the slice, and through
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfTerminalSection` at the terminal object `𝟙_U` of the
slice. Both are determined by their values, and those are the same restriction. -/
theorem globalSectionOfSection_eq_globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
    (U : X.C) (a : X.O.obj.obj (op U)) :
    globalSectionOfSection X U a =
      globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal a := by
  refine (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).injective (Subtype.ext (funext fun V => ?_))
  show globalSectionVal (globalSectionOfSection X U a) V =
    globalSectionVal (globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal a) V
  refine (globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSection X U a V).trans
    (Eq.trans ?_ (globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U)
      Over.mkIdTerminal a V).symm)
  exact congrArg (fun h : unop V ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 U) => ((X.over U).O.obj.map h.op).hom a)
    (Over.mkIdTerminal.hom_ext (Over.homMk (unop V).hom) (Over.mkIdTerminal.from (unop V)))

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **The ringed-site and ringed-space models of `RΓ(U, -)` are the same functor** on the small
Zariski site of a scheme: both are the total right derived functor of sections over `U` with
values in modules over `Γ(X, U)`, and the two spellings of the structure sheaf of rings are
definitionally equal. [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] is stated in the first model and
[Stacks, Tag 0A0L] in the second. -/
theorem derivedSectionsOverObject_eq_derivedSections (X : Scheme.{u}) (U : X.Opens) :
    RingedSite.derivedSectionsOverObject (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite X.sheaf) U =
      derivedSections (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) U :=
  rfl

/-! ### The Čech completion is every reflector -/

/-- **Any left adjoint of the inclusion of the derived-complete objects of `D(A)`, composed with
that inclusion, is the Čech completion functor** of [Stacks, Tag 091V] at a finite family
spanning the ideal.

The Čech completion is a reflection onto the derived-complete objects —
`CechCompletion.cechCompletion_isReflection` — and the three conditions of
`Stacks.Algebraization.leftAdjointCompιIsoOfCompletionFunctor` are read off its universal
property: the unit is invertible at a complete object because precomposition with it is
bijective there, and the completion functor inverts its own unit because, again by bijectivity,
`Φ(η_K) = η_{Φ K}`. Two left adjoints of one functor are isomorphic, which moves the
identification from `ι.leftAdjoint` to an arbitrary `C`. -/
theorem cechCompletionFunctor_iso_compι (A : Type u) [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    [HasProductsOfShape ℕ (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A))]
    {C : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) ⥤
      (show ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) from
        fun L => IsDerivedComplete (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) L).FullSubcategory}
    (a : C ⊣ (show ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) from
      fun L => IsDerivedComplete (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) L).ι) :
    Nonempty (C ⋙ (show ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) from
        fun L => IsDerivedComplete (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) L).ι ≅
      DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A f) := by
  obtain ⟨η, hcomplete, hbij⟩ := CechCompletion.cechCompletion_isReflection A f
  have hunit : ∀ Z : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A),
      IsDerivedComplete (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) Z → IsIso (η.app Z) := by
    intro Z hZ
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (hbij Z Z hZ).surjective (𝟙 Z)
    have hs' : η.app Z ≫ s = 𝟙 Z := hs
    refine ⟨s, hs', ?_⟩
    refine (hbij Z _ (hcomplete Z)).injective ?_
    show η.app Z ≫ s ≫ η.app Z = η.app Z ≫ 𝟙 _
    rw [← Category.assoc, hs']
    simp
  have hmap : ∀ Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A),
      IsIso ((DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A f).map (η.app Y)) := by
    intro Y
    have hnat : η.app Y ≫ η.app ((CechCompletion.cechCompletionFunctor A f).obj Y) =
        η.app Y ≫ (CechCompletion.cechCompletionFunctor A f).map (η.app Y) :=
      η.naturality (η.app Y)
    have key : η.app ((CechCompletion.cechCompletionFunctor A f).obj Y) =
        (CechCompletion.cechCompletionFunctor A f).map (η.app Y) :=
      (hbij Y _ (hcomplete ((CechCompletion.cechCompletionFunctor A f).obj Y))).injective hnat
    rw [show (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A f).map (η.app Y) =
        (CechCompletion.cechCompletionFunctor A f).map (η.app Y) from rfl, ← key]
    exact hunit _ (hcomplete Y)
  have : (show ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) from
      fun L => IsDerivedComplete (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) L).ι.IsRightAdjoint := ⟨⟨C, ⟨a⟩⟩⟩
  exact ⟨Functor.isoWhiskerRight
      (a.leftAdjointUniq (Adjunction.ofIsRightAdjoint _)) _ ≪≫
    leftAdjointCompιIsoOfCompletionFunctor η hcomplete hunit hmap⟩

/-- **The derived completion functor along a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals of a locally
Noetherian scheme**, as an instance. This is [Stacks, Tag 099F],
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete`, at the finite-type ideal sheaf
`Stacks.Algebraization.isFiniteType_idealSheafSiteSubmodule` supplies; it is recorded as an
instance at this shape because instance search does not chain through the finite-type step on its
own, and without it the object `K^∧` cannot be written down in a statement. -/
instance isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealSheafSiteSubmodule (X : Scheme.{u})
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
      (idealSheafSiteSubmodule I))).IsRightAdjoint :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete _ _

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
